/* Deep lessons — Dasturlash asoslari (programming-basics).
 *
 * Written for somebody who has never written a line of C++: every idea is
 * motivated before it is named, every piece of code is walked line by line,
 * and every mechanism a beginner cannot see (the input stream cursor, the
 * bits inside an int, the copy a function makes) is drawn or stepped through.
 *
 * Original text. The teaching order follows what a strong competitive
 * programming curriculum covers, but no sentence, picture or example is
 * copied from any source.
 */

